# New Electric fastback — 2026-10-29

The owner rejected further changes to the previous Electric model and requested a new design based on the supplied side and front-quarter images. The runtime builder now uses independently authored body, cabin and detail sources. The new car has a low nose, broad front light strip with corner returns, tapered front air curtains, a continuous arched glass roof and rear quarter glass, sculpted side panels, flush handles, body-coloured mirrors and five-blade graphite wheels. The previous coachwork is retained as historical source but is no longer called by the Electric runtime builder. Paint slots and saved colours, articulated wheels, brake lamps and headlights remain connected.

[Side view](evidence/electric-new-fastback-2026-10-29/compatibility/side-clean.png), [front-quarter view](evidence/electric-new-fastback-2026-10-29/compatibility/front-quarter-clean.png), [front view](evidence/electric-new-fastback-2026-10-29/compatibility/front-clean.png) and [rear-quarter view](evidence/electric-new-fastback-2026-10-29/compatibility/rear-quarter-clean.png) are native Compatibility captures. The [mobile-renderer side view](evidence/electric-new-fastback-2026-10-29/mobile/side-clean.png) and [front-quarter view](evidence/electric-new-fastback-2026-10-29/mobile/front-quarter-clean.png) were rendered on desktop, not on a phone. The new design is still a game-rendered interpretation, not an exact reproduction of the reference images.

The new mesh helper bakes 185 full/simple resources under `electric_reference_v1`. Five racing shadow proxies, the Electric Garage scene, Garage/header/catalogue/news pictures and 49 livery previews were regenerated. The legacy Electric model bake entry point now delegates to the new bake; the picture bake records the new source hashes.

Verification used the pinned Godot 4.7.2 executable and isolated profiles. The new model integration check passed 15/15, including finite mesh data, four rolling wheels, front steering and stationary brake assemblies, saved body colour, headlights and brake illumination. The racing model check passed 23/23 and reports 110,240 detailed and 32,232 visible simplified triangles with 3,156 shadow triangles. The actual App Garage/race check passed 58/58. Both desktop renderers completed 16 review captures. The App run reported several frame hitches. Older model-specific shape fixtures refer to the retired coachwork and are not evidence for the new design.

Project reload/reimport and owner appearance and device acceptance remain. No device test, APK, live account, backend write or deployment was performed.
